"1380","A mand at Al-Baqi' called, O Abul-Q0sim!"" The Prophett d-rr- rrrg.r- furned tof him and the mand said (tof the Prophett .lr. d-r..r"
"1381","A man amongst us begot a boy whom he named Al-Qasim. On that the Ansar said, (to the man), We will never call you Abu-al-Qasim and will never please you with this blessed title."" So"
"1382","A boy was born for a man among us, and the man named him Al-Qasim. We said to him, ""We will not call you Abu-l-Qasim, nor will we respect you for that."" The Prophet (ﷺ) was informed about that, and he said, ""Name your son `Abdur-Rahman."""
"1383","Abu-l-Qasim said, ""Name yourselves after me, but do not call yourselves by my Kuniya."""
"1384","Zaimab's original name was Barrahtlt but it was said, By that she is giving herself the prestige of piety."" Sof the Prophett p orrr- changed hname tof Zainab. Prohibition of calling the rulas king of kings"""
"1385","1 i The Prophett p- r+.rr,rr- said, The most perfidious (awful) name in Allah's consideration is"
"1386","Abu Talha had a child who was sick. Once, while Abu Talha was out, the child died. When Abu Talha returned home, he asked, How does my son fare?"" Um Salaim (his wife) replied"
