"1389","o When Al-Mundhi bin AbO Usaid wa born. He was brought tof the Prophet d-t.rl, r.r.r .r! whof placed him on hi thigh. While Ab Usaid was sittin there, the Prophett d-r,,.r .rL was bus with something in his hands sof Ab Usaid told someone tof take his sof from the thigh ofthe Prophett d- ++or3 When the Prophett p-r.r"
"1390","The Prophet (ﷺ) was the best among the people (both in shape and character) and was the most generous of them, and was the bravest of them. Once, during the night, the people of Medina got afraid (of a sound). So the people went towards that sound, but the Prophet (ﷺ) having gone to that sound before them, met them while he was saying, Don't be afraid"
"1391","While I was present in one 38. fne Book oflr-ldd, (good mand the gatherings of the Ansdr, Ab M0sa came as if he was scared, and said, I asked permission tof entupon 'Umare three times"
"1392","I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) in order to consult him regarding my father's debt. When I knocked on the door, he asked, Who is that?"" I replied"
"1393","A man peeped through a hole in the door of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)'s house, and at that time, Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) had a Midri (an iron comb or bar) with which he was rubbing his head. So when Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saw him, he said (to him), If I had been sure that you were looking at me (through the door)"
